    {
      "id": "fe863e96e1ec3aabb23e10718eb195e14d89705a",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2703502868,
          "type": null,
          "body": "This causes a crash when a field is current selected and then dissection changes, e.g., from right-clicking on a preference in the proto tree, like \"Reassemble out-of-order segments\" in TCP.\n\nI believe it's because when the redissection is triggered `DataSourceTab::byteViewTextMarked` is being called before `DataSourceTab::selectedFrameChanged`, and thus `edt_` has not yet been set to NULL, but is in fact point to the old, destroyed `epan_dissect_t` and Bad Stuff Happens.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-08-22T13:54:03.447Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-08-22T13:54:03.447Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 407408465,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20898,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "e3f1d933ee0fce100a7b1eb42885f93f042a362f",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2703533781,
          "type": null,
          "body": "In `DataSourceTab::selectedFrameChanged` the `clear();` gets called before the \"check to see if the `edt_` has gone away, and the `clear()` ends up calling the `leaveEvent`.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-08-22T14:05:42.804Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-08-22T14:05:42.804Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 407408465,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20898,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2244167a2834105e13cddcbb8666f197551ede83",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2703577886,
          "type": null,
          "body": "It's a little unclear to me if the `clear()` needs to be called if the children are deleted right afterwards. (Though we still might want to set the `edt_` to null first.)\n\n*edit*: It seems with testing that indeed we don't need to call `clear()` if we delete the children, probably(?) because the parenting relationship is set up correctly.\n\nAlso: https://stackoverflow.com/a/76848495",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-08-22T14:17:05.400Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-08-22T14:46:40.241Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 407408465,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20898,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4e01e3a8fe6c50bccdb18a80fab970600103b1a4",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2703681458,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "So either in `DataSourceTab::selectedFrameChanged` we can comment out the `clear()` call, we can move the check that sets `edt_` to nullptr if necessary before the clear and delete, or we can do both.",
